{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I checked your account and it's in good standing: it's active, VPN access is enabled, and your Duo sign-in is set up. Our records also show your VPN sign-ins from Lisbon over the last few days went through successfully, so the problem is most likely on the laptop or the hotel Wi-Fi rather than your account. Please try these steps: 1) Open a web browser and go to any public website. If it doesn't load, the hotel Wi-Fi sign-in page probably needs to be accepted first. Complete that page, then try again. 2) Fully quit the VPN client, reopen it, and connect. Approve the Duo push on your phone when it arrives. If the push doesn't arrive, open Duo Mobile and pull down to refresh. 3) If it still fails, restart your laptop and try once more. Then reply with the exact error message the VPN client shows, and whether a Duo prompt appeared. If it still won't connect, we'll escalate it to our second-line team right away so you can get to the shared drive for your presentation.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-net-01, user Leo Martins (user_id 6, Sales, home TZ America/New_York). lookup_user: status active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0. Triage said user_blocked true, but the account record shows it is not blocked; the triage value looks wrong, so I did not treat this as a security block. check_mfa_status: Duo push enrolled. check_signin_logs (last 14 days): 10 VPN/M365 sign-ins, all success, 0 failed_password, 0 mfa_denied. Lisbon VPN successes on 2026-10-08, 10-09, and 10-10 (residential IP 198.51.100.66). No server-side failure found, so per KB-013 this is client or hotel Wi-Fi side. No fix actions were requested. Asked user for the exact error text and Duo behavior. Next step if they still fail: escalate to Tier 2 with the error message and the Lisbon sign-in evidence. Shared drive access is not a permissions issue, so KB-006 does not apply. KB-016 applies once VPN connects.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-016"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
